This project ports parts of brother-scand to Rust:
https://github.com/pietern/brother-scand (fork of https://github.com/darsto/brother-scand)

  - data_channel.c: write_scan_params, data_channel_send_scan_params,
    exchange_params2 -> src/lib.rs command(), the ESC I / ESC X requests and
    parse_i_reply()
  - data_channel.c: data_channel_init_connection -> the greeting check in scan_to()
  - data_channel.c: process_header, process_chunk_header,
    process_page_end_header, process_scan_end_header (pietern), and the
    single-byte status case in process_header (darsto) -> receive()
  - config.c: default scan parameters (B, N, D, G, L, C, M) -> the ESC X fields
  - rle_to_tiff.py: rle_decode -> PackBits::feed; also copied unchanged except
    for added type hints into parity/rle/rle.py as the recorded original

